                <pb facs="0818" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4330: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-04T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 4—8:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>195. My 193, May 4, 1 p.m. Wu’s forces following up their victory over Chang’s
                    forces at Changhsintien at 5 o’clock this morning occupied at noon district of
                    Fengtai on Peking-Tientsin Railway. Chang’s forces left many dead and wounded
                    and many guns behind.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
